A||||2||mrfixit58||Dew Wipe Help!!!||||5||
Z||000000||mrfixit58||07-14-2000||10:19 PM||||Well, it's after 10:00 pm and I've been struggling with the dew wipe on the passenger side for about 2 1/2 hours. I made a little screwdriver like Rodney sells and it worked to remove the screws. I've got the new dew wipe in but can't get one of the screws in. It the second one from the door latch end. What hints can you lend to me to help me out?<P>Thanks in advance,<BR>Roy||||reg||5
Z||000001||tgowens||07-14-2000||11:27 PM||||Hey Roy,<P>those things are a bear, aren't they??? One thing I did was just to hold the screw lightly with a pair of needle-nose pliers until I got the screw started, then I just gently turned it with the "dew wipe tool" until it was in.........it's a simple but tedious way of doing it but it worked for me!<P>------------------<BR>     '87 Fiero GT<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/3D_sig.gif">            <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gokart||07-15-2000||06:48 AM||||Go to the hardware store and replace those screws with stainless steel metric head bolts with matching threads! That's what I did so it'll be so much easier the next time I have to replace them. I started mine with one of those long antenna magnets they sell at the counter at Autozone(best $1.50 I ever spent). Just put the bolt at the end and slip it in and turn it in there enough to get it to stay in then a small wrench will take care of the rest! Who's got that tool I made and was being passed around anyway? Hope it gets passed around to everyone who needs it <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> Marc                     87GT||||reg||4
